    "result_text": "The full test suite is just the acceptance test (the other two files are a base class and helper). Everything is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `namesakeCount` on owner creation \u2014 the count of existing owners sharing the same first and last name (case-insensitively) *before* the new owner is persisted.\n\nChanges:\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 computes and sets the count before saving, via a new `namesakeCount(firstName, lastName)` helper that reuses the existing `normalizeIdentity` (trim + collapse whitespace + lower-case) for the case-insensitive comparison against `findAllOwners()`, consistent with the household/telephone duplicate checks.\n- **`Owner` model** \u2014 added a persisted `namesake_count` column with getter/setter (the value is read back on `GET /api/owners/{id}`).\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `namesakeCount` (int32, min 0) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it by name automatically.\n- **schema.sql** (hsqldb/h2/postgres/mysql) \u2014 added the `namesake_count` column.\n\n`mvn test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The test creates two owners with the same first/last name (different addresses to avoid the household 409) and asserts the second reports `namesakeCount = 1`.",
